+## Loop names (#209)
+
+The API refuses a loop name that another of the owner's loops holds after trimming, collapsing whitespace runs and lowercasing (`409 LOOP_NAME_CONFLICT` with an advisory `suggestedName`; [ADR-0073](decisions/ADR-0073-transactional-loop-names.md), docs/07). The UI never retries on its own and never creates a copy under a name the user did not submit. Every surface says which name was refused and the rule ("Names that differ only in letter case or spacing count as the same name."), keeps everything that existed, and makes the next attempt a deliberate submission. `lib/loop-names.ts` reads the refusal only from the exact code and a non-blank string `suggestedName`, and mirrors the comparison key solely to decide whether a field still holds the refused name (the API decides admission). A suggestion can be taken before the retry: the API then refuses again with a fresh suggestion (derived from the attempted name, for example "X copy copy"), which the same guidance shows. `400 LOOP_NAME_INVALID` keeps the ordinary error text.
+
+- **Create** (Loops). The refusal is the field's error: under **New loop name**, `role="alert"`, `aria-invalid` and `aria-describedby` on the input, with **Use “suggestion”** below (`LoopNameTakenHelp`). The button replaces the text and returns focus to the field; **Create** or Enter is the retry. The guidance follows the field's text: it hides when the text no longer matches the refused name and returns if it matches again. Other refusals keep their existing message.
+- **Import** (Loops). The parsed upload is held unchanged and the refusal opens a full-width region, **Import under another name**, on its own line below the Create and Import row so the Create form never moves. It holds a warning (`<file> was not imported`, the name, the rule, and that neither the file nor the existing loop changes) and `LoopNameRetryForm`: **Name for the imported loop**, prefilled with the suggestion, focused and selected so Enter accepts and typing replaces, then **Import as new loop** and **Cancel**. Each retry calls `loops.import(client, originalDocument, { name })`: the same body, the name in the query. A raced name shows under the field as an alert with the new suggestion, and focus stays where it was. Another failure keeps the form and shows its reason, adding "check the loop list" only when the request may have committed (no answer or 5xx). **Cancel** returns focus to the file picker; choosing another file starts over. The picker is described by the warning while it is shown.
+- **Template copies** (gallery). A refused **Use** creates nothing and the card's action area becomes the same form: a warning (**Name the new <template> draft**: the template's name is taken, the rule, and that loops and the template are unchanged), **Name for the new draft** prefilled with the suggestion and focused, **Create draft** and **Cancel**. **Create draft** sends the existing `name` field of the draft request under the gallery's single in-flight guard (`aria-disabled`, `aria-busy`, polite status), then opens the editor as before. **Cancel** restores **Use** and focuses it. A successful copy clears the card's form. The first refusal names no spelling because the API chose the template's own name; later refusals name the submitted one.
+- **Rename** (editor). A refused draft save keeps the draft exactly as typed: the editor store records `nameConflict` (refused name, suggestion), the save state reads **Not saved: name in use** with the warning icon, and **Another loop already has this name** (a polite status, `NameConflictNotice`) appears above the canvas. It says where the changes are (this device, this window only, or this editor while the device write runs) and that the server keeps the previous name and draft; its actions are **Use “suggestion”** (one undoable rename step of its own; focus then moves to the save status), **Edit name** (expands Loop settings and focuses and selects **Name**, which is `aria-invalid` and described by the refusal without a second announcement) and **Try again** (sends the same name once, `aria-busy` while pending, for when the other loop was renamed; a repeat refusal adds "It was still in use when tried again."). While the draft still has the refused name, autosave mirrors every edit to the device but sends nothing, the save on leaving the editor is skipped, and **Publish** refuses with "Another loop already has this name; choose a different name before publishing." Changing the name lets the next save go; an accepted save clears the refusal. A load (navigation, reload, Reload server draft) clears it; reopening the editor restores this device's unsynced copy and its save asks again. Inside the node dialog, where the page is inert, the notice appears in the dialog without **Edit name** and says to close the dialog first; there, taking the suggestion moves focus to the dialog's title.
+- **Existing duplicates.** The UI performs no conversion. A store with equivalent names from an earlier build stops at startup; the CHANGELOG's upgrade note gives the manual repair in the previous build or an explicit reset.
+- **Regression.** `lib/loop-names.test.ts`, `loops/loop-names.test.tsx` (Create, Import and template copies against the fake API's admission rule, including original-document retries and raced suggestions), `editor/EditorPage.name-conflict.test.tsx` (device copy, held saves, undo, Edit name focus, Try again, stale-draft precedence, the node dialog, and leaving and returning), and Edge `e2e/loop-names.spec.ts` and `e2e/template-gallery.spec.ts`. The shared E2E gateway keeps one store for the whole run, so fixtures that repeat a name pass it through `uniqueLoopName` in `e2e/fixtures.ts`.
