+The Loops page's **New from template** action opens the installed catalog. Each card shows its description, tags and one green **Use &lt;template name&gt;** button. Using it immediately creates an ordinary independent draft and opens the editor. When one of the owner's loops already has the template's name, the card asks for a name instead (see "Loop names"); the gallery gains no other fields. The gallery has no settings form, repository or GitHub URL field, prerequisite report, readiness presentation or configured-automation action. It does not fetch model choices or harness preflight for setup. Prompts consume the run's input and existing context; instructions, variables, model choices, limits and working directory can be configured in the copied loop. Cards share intrinsic grid rows so descriptions, tags and primary actions stay aligned across siblings and wrap at narrow widths.
 
 A synchronous in-flight guard prevents repeated draft creation across cards while creation or editor handoff is pending. Pending controls stay focusable with `aria-disabled` and `aria-busy`, and a polite status announces progress. A failed creation shows an alert and refreshes the loop list without automatically retrying a request that might already have committed. A navigation failure after successful creation retains the loop ID: the same **Use** button retries opening that draft, and the alert offers an editor link. The loop opens with normal undo, autosave, validation and publication behavior. Default canvas spacing and layout persistence follow their separate backlog issues #124/#125.
 
